      "title": "Introduction to Trigonometry",
      "renderer": "manim",
      "narration": "Welcome to the fascinating world of trigonometry! The word itself comes from Greek words 'trigonon', meaning triangle, and 'metron', meaning measure. At its core, trigonometry is the branch of mathematics that studies the relationships between the sides and angles of triangles. This might sound simple, but it's an incredibly powerful tool with applications everywhere, from building bridges and video games to astronomy and navigation. Imagine trying to find the height of a tall mountain without climbing it, or a ship trying to determine its distance from the shore. Trigonometry makes these seemingly impossible calculations possible. In this chapter, we will begin our journey by focusing on the fundamental building block of trigonometry: the right-angled triangle. We will learn about specific ratios of the sides of these triangles, called trigonometric ratios, which are the foundation for everything else that follows. Get ready to see triangles in a whole new light!",
