          "wan_prompt": "Flat vector illustration, bright colors, Indian educational textbook style, purple and blue gradient background. Three primary ratios (Sin, Cos, Tan) are shown as solid blocks. With a flipping animation, they turn over to reveal their reciprocals (Csc, Sec, Cot) on the other side. For example, the 'Sin' block with the fraction 'O/H' flips over to become a 'Csc' block with the fraction 'H/O'. Arrows connect the pairs to show the relationship.",
          "narration": "Beyond the main three, there are three more ratios called reciprocal ratios: Cosecant, Secant, and Cotangent. The best way to think of them is as 'flipping friends'. Cosecant is just the sine ratio flipped upside down. Secant is the cosine ratio flipped over. And Cotangent is the tangent ratio flipped. You don't need to memorize six different formulas from scratch; if you know SOH CAH TOA, you automatically know the other three just by inverting the fractions. They always come in these pairs."
        },
        {
          "scene": 4,
