          "narration": "The real power of trigonometry comes when you combine these tools. If you're given a right triangle with some information—like one side and one angle, or two sides—you can solve for everything else. First, see if you can use SOH CAH TOA. If you're missing a side needed for the ratio, use Pythagoras to find it first. By switching between the trigonometric ratios and the Pythagorean theorem, no right-angled triangle can hide its secrets from you. You have a complete toolkit to solve them all."
